  "question": {
    "text": "If the set of all $\\mathrm{a} \\in \\mathbf{R}$, for which the equation $2 x^2+(a-5) x+15=3 \\mathrm{a}$ has no real root, is the interval $(\\alpha, \\beta)$, and $X=\\{x \\in Z: \\alpha \\lt x \\lt \\beta\\}$, then $\\sum_{x \\in X} x^2$ is equal to :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "2109",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "2129",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "2119",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "2139",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & (a-5)^2-8(15-3 a) < 0 \\\\ & a^2+14 a+25-120 < 0 \\\\ & a^2+14 a-95 < 0 \\\\ & (a+19)(a-5) < 0 \\\\ & a \\in(-19,5) \\\\ & \\therefore-19 < x < 5 \\\\ & \\therefore \\sum_{x \\in X} x^2=\\left(1^2+2^2+\\ldots .+4^2\\right)+\\left(1^2+2^2+\\ldots+18^2\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{4 \\times 5 \\times 9}{6}+\\frac{18 \\times 19 \\times 37}{6} \\\\ & =30+2109 \\\\ & =2139\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}